  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises to adopt new business models, technology and techniques to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In April 2020 the Ministry of Industry and Commerce announced the official use of of the Laos In Business Training modules as the official package that Micro Small and Medium Enterprises need to complete in order to access reduced interest rate loans from Government financing. 

At the end of 2021, Lao PDR has a package of &#x2018;Resilient Micro Small and Medium Enterprises&apos; training tools which have been developed and tested to support the capacity development of the Lao MSMEs. These training tools are added onto the already ongoing Government Capacity building support in a delivery model which is low cost, and has ownership by the leading Business Development Service Providers.
 ILO has continued providing both resource mobilization and technical support to this important national initiative through the newly funded 
&#x2018;Supporting Lao Micro Small and Medium Enterprises resilience in response to Covid19 project&quot; with funding from the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation. 

In February, the ILO handed over the Laos IN Business training package to both Lao National Chamber of Commerce and Industry and the Ministry of Industry and Commerce and jointly they supported Micro Small and Medium Enterprises in accessing finance. 

The ILO helped to create a &#x2018;one stop&apos; information portal for all Micro Small and Medium Enterprises support in Laos, to be managed by the Small and Medium Enterprise Service Centre.</narrative>
   </description>
